       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 2400 mg four times daily comes to **9,600 mg/day**. The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 2,400 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nYou may have meant a **total daily dose of 2,400 mg**. Here are some common regimens that add up to that:\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally with your supervising resident or attending. I'll enter the order once you do. If you do intend the original dose, it needs to be reviewed and confirmed by your supervising physician first."
